%N A374091 a(n) is the smallest nonnegative integer k where exactly n ordered pairs of positive integers (x, y) exist such that x^2 + 3*x*y + y^2 = k.
%C A374091 a(n) is the smallest nonnegative k such that A374089(k) = n.
%C A374091 a(n) is of the form 5*k^2 if and only if n is odd.
%C A374091 a(21) = 3197667605. - _Chai Wah Wu_, Jun 29 2024
%C A374091 a(27) = 183678605. - _Chai Wah Wu_, Jun 28 2024
%H A374091 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A374091/b374091.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..966</a>
%F A374091 a(2*n) = A374095(n).
%F A374091 a(n) <= 5*11^(n-1) for all n >= 1. - _Jason Yuen_, Jun 29 2024
